flowchart TB
  accTitle: B4 authority and method-governance architecture
  accDescr: The principal establishes the goal and invariants. A goal store and intention registry preserve versions and rationale. Monitors emit evidence-bound events; diagnosis supports a governor decision. The governor can continue, switch method, delegate, suspend, or abandon within policy. A separate authorization gate controls dispatch. Model proposals and delegated results are inputs, not authority sources.
  P[Principal / authorized policy] --> G[Goal authority adapter]
  G --> GS[Versioned goal store]
  GS --> IR[Persistent intention registry]
  IR --> X[Execution monitor]
  X --> EV[Validated reconsideration event]
  EV --> D[Diagnosis and evidence]
  MP[Model method proposal] --> D
  DR[Delegated result] --> D
  D --> GOV[Method governor]
  GOV -->|continue or switch| IR
  GOV -->|delegate| DL[Scoped child task]
  GOV -->|suspend or abandon| IR
  GOV --> AG[Authorization gate]
  MR[Method registry] --> AG
  AG --> EX[Executor and outbox]
  EX --> X
  GOV --> AL[Audit and outcome ledger]
  IR --> AL
  EX --> AL
